# Every text file is checked out with LF line ends, on every host.
#
# Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. A shell script or
# a Dockerfile copied into a Linux image then carries a carriage return on every
# line and fails there, and every file hashed into an image tag hashes to other
# bytes than on Linux. `text=auto` leaves binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
